# A Git origin stages a plain worktree: the directory a recipe is handed holds the checked-out sources and no
# repository, so a walk of it never meets a file git is still creating and removing. The recipe copies the worktree
# and builds libanswer out of the copy, so the binary printing 42 proves the copy holds the sources at the pinned tag.
> setupRepo
> Compile/snxConfig
> checkWorktree
> run
